{"name":"Hidden Hills","hex":"#c5d2b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hidden Hills","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Los Angeles County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hidden_Hills"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hidden Hills","blocks":[{"text":"Hidden Hills is an American sitcom television series that aired on NBC from September 24, 2002, to January 21, 2003, during the 2002 fall line-up. Based on the book Surviving Suburbia, the series was created by Peter Segal and Ric Swartzlander. The theme song was \"Pleasant Valley Sunday\", made famous by The Monkees. Mark Mothersbaugh performed the version used on the show. The show was made by Ric Swartzlander's Rude Mood Productions and NBC."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_Hills","wikidata":"Q5751834"},{"title":"Hill","blocks":[{"text":"A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG/330px-Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill","wikidata":"Q54050"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG/500px-Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG/500px-Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Puijo Hill in Kuopio, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_